## Why This Question Matters

This question assesses your understanding of end-to-end data isolation, cross-region replication, retention governance, and PII redaction across a data lake, transformed layers, and BI dashboards—essential skills for building enterprise-compliant multi-tenant systems.

## Key Concepts to Demonstrate

- Multi-tenant data isolation across raw and transformed layers
- Per-tenant retention and purge workflows with full auditability
- Cross-region replication latency and consistency guarantees
- PII redaction verification across caches and dashboards
- Seed data design and deterministic testing signals

## Code Example

```javascript
// Seed tenants for deterministic E2E tests
const tenants = [
  { id: 't1', name: 'Acme Corp', region: 'us-east-1' },
  { id: 't2', name: 'Globex', region: 'eu-west-1' }
];

// Simulate event streams from mobile and web
async function seedEventStream(tenant, source) {
  const events = generateEvents(tenant.id, source, 1000);
  await publishToIngestTopic(tenant.region, events);
}

// Verify isolation: ensure t1 cannot access t2 data
async function verifyIsolation() {
  const t1Raw = await queryRawLake('t1');
  const t2Raw = await queryRawLake('t2');
  expect(t1Raw).not.toContainTenantData('t2');
  expect(t2Raw).not.toContainTenantData('t1');
}

// Verify PII redaction in transformed views
async function verifyRedaction() {
  const transformed = await queryTransformedView('t1');
  expect(transformed).toHaveRedacted('email');
  expect(transformed).toHaveRedacted('phone');
}
```

## Verification Matrix

| Layer | Isolation | Redaction | Retention |
|-------|-----------|-----------|------------|
| Raw Lake | ✓ | N/A | ✓ |
| Transformed | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Cache | ✓ | ✓ | N/A |
| BI Dashboard | ✓ | ✓ | N/A |

## Essential Metrics

- **Isolation violations**: Zero cross-tenant data leaks
- **Redaction coverage**: 100% of defined PII fields
- **Replication lag**: < 5s for sync, < 60s for async regions
- **Retention accuracy**: Auto-purge at tenant-specified TTL
- **Query latency**: P95 < 500ms for dashboard queries

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical E2E testing skills for beginners: data seeding, mocking remote services (feature flags), validating UI variants, and ensuring idempotent events within a fintech onboarding flow.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and remote config
- Test data seeding and isolation
- API interception/mocking
- Idempotent event verification
- Variant-driven UI testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Cypress skeleton for onboarding with feature flag
describe('Onboarding feature flag', () => {
  const userId = 'test-user-001';
  beforeEach(() => {
    cy.request('POST', '/test/setup-user', { userId });
  });

  it('Variant A renders steps A1/A2', () => {
    cy.intercept('/api/flags', { variant: 'A' }).as('flagA');
    cy.visit('/onboarding');
    cy.wait('@flagA');
    cy.get('.step1').should('be.visible');
  });

  it('Idempotent event when flag toggled', () => {
    cy.intercept('/api/flags', { variant: 'A' }).as('flagA');
    cy.visit('/onboarding');
    // complete some steps
    cy.reload(); // simulate flag refresh
    cy.intercept('/api/flags', { variant: 'B' }).as('flagB');
    cy.wait('@flagB');
    cy.get('@onlyOnboardingEvent').should('have.length', 1);
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to more than two variants and ensure coverage of each path?
- How would you integrate this with CI to catch flakey flag-based flows?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests for real-time collaboration systems must handle offline edits, eventual consistency, and deterministic merges. This question evaluates your ability to architect an end-to-end flow that exercises offline queues, CRDT-based merging, and version history while ensuring test isolation and reproducibility.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first collaboration with optimistic UI updates
- CRDT-based merge algorithms ensuring deterministic outcomes
- Test data isolation using per-test seeds and unique identifiers
- Server-sync mocks with controlled timing for deterministic test results

## Code Example

```javascript
// Setup two Playwright contexts for concurrent user simulation
const contextA = await browser.newContext();
const contextB = await browser.newContext();
const pageA = await contextA.newPage();
const pageB = await contextB.newPage();

// Seed a shared base document
const docId = await seedDocument({ content: 'Initial paragraph.' });

// Simulate offline for both users
await setNetworkOffline(pageA);
await setNetworkOffline(pageB);

// User A edits the paragraph
await pageA.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageA.locator('.editor').fill('User A edited this.');

// User B edits the same paragraph offline
await pageB.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageB.locator('.editor').fill('User B edited that.');

// Reconnect both users to trigger CRDT sync
await setNetworkOnline(pageA);
await setNetworkOnline(pageB);

// Wait for sync completion
await expect(pageA.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');
await expect(pageB.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');

// Verify idempotent replay
const versionBefore = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
await triggerSyncAgain(pageA);
const versionAfter = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
expect(versionAfter).toBe(versionBefore);

// Verify version history
const history = await getVersionHistory(docId);
expect(history).toContain('User A edited this.');
expect(history).toContain('User B edited that.');
```
